`src/text_mate_backend/readability/` is a Python port of the built-in
readability analyzer of blokkli/editor:

  - src/modules/readability/runtime/analyzers/builtin.ts
  - src/modules/readability/runtime/analyzers/builtin.spec.ts
  - src/runtime/editor/features/analyze/readability/types.ts

Ported: the analyzer contract; the tokenization helpers (`getWords`,
`getSentences`, `sentenceCount`, `wordCount`, `longWordCount`, `charCount`,
`avgSentenceLength`, `avgSyllablesPerWord`, `polysyllableCount`); the Flesch
Reading Ease, LIX and Gulpease formulas; the `fleschToCefr` mapping; and the
per-language `SCORE_CONFIGS` calibration (bands, impact thresholds, minimum word
counts and score reference tables) for `en`, `fr` and `it`. The expectations of
`builtin.spec.ts` are ported as test vectors in `tests/test_readability_*.py`.

Not ported: the Wiener Sachtextformel and the `countSyllablesDe` heuristic —
German is scored with ZIX instead (see below).

