German readability is scored with ZIX, a trained model published by the
Statistisches Amt des Kantons Zürich. It is used as a dependency (see
`pyproject.toml`), not vendored. The German target band (ZIX >= 0, i.e. CEFR
A1/A2/B1) follows the calibration in `machinelearningZH/simply-simplify-language`
(`config.yaml`: `limit_hard: 0`, `limit_medium: -2`).

